  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "This serves 6 and takes about 1 hour 20 minutes. The thing to watch is the tomato sauce stage: cook it hard over high heat until it reduces to a thick, deep-red paste. This concentrates the flavour and removes the raw tomato taste before the rice goes in."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Ghanaian jollof traditionally uses long-grain or basmati rice. Wash it well until the water runs clear or the excess starch will make it clump and go sticky."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
